    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "overview",
      "narration_text": "AI research tools are everywhere now for market and academic summaries. The problem is every finding comes out sounding equally confident, whether it is a well sourced fact or a fabricated statistic.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.25,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · STEM/AI",
            "segment": "Spotting Unreliable AI Research",
            "command": "Why do AI research answers all sound equally confident?",
            "runningText": "checking sources…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "A fabricated statistic looks as sure as a well-sourced fact."
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-24T17:23:35.350974+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "render_duration_s": 13.266666666666667,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-09-24T13:38:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "framework-1",
      "narration_text": "The first check is recency. Ask when this claim was actually true. An AI answer can quote a real number from years ago and present it as today's fact, so I always ask the tool, or myself, how current this specific figure really is.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.32,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · STEM/AI",
            "segment": "Check 1: Recency",
            "command": "Check 1: is this current, or stale?",
            "runningText": "checking the date…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "An old number presented as today's fact is the #1 tell."
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-24T17:24:36.248675+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "render_duration_s": 15.333333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-09-24T13:38:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "framework-2",
      "narration_text": "The second check is source authority. A confident sentence is not a citation. I trace every claim back to where it originated, and I weigh a primary source, like a filing or a dataset, far above a summary of a summary with no link at all.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.4,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · STEM/AI",
            "segment": "Source Authority",
            "command": "Check 2: where did this claim actually come from?",
            "runningText": "tracing the source…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "A confident sentence is not a citation."
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-24T17:34:54.832839+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "render_duration_s": 15.4,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-09-24T13:38:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "framework-3",
      "narration_text": "The third check is corroboration. One source, however official it sounds, is one opinion. I look for a second and third independent source that agree before I treat a number as settled, and if I cannot find one, I flag the claim as unconfirmed.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.96,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · STEM/AI",
            "segment": "Check 3: Corroboration",
            "command": "Check 3: does more than one source agree?",
            "runningText": "cross-checking…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "One confident source is still just one opinion."
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-24T17:26:39.839081+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "render_duration_s": 15.966666666666667,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-09-24T13:38:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "takeaway",
      "narration_text": "So the next time an AI tool hands you a confident sounding answer, run these three checks: is it recent, is the source authoritative, and does another source agree. That is a concrete habit you can start using on your very next AI search.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.36,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "Your turn.",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · STEM/AI",
            "segment": "The Checklist",
            "command": "Run this 3-check habit on your next AI search.",
            "runningText": "building the checklist…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "Recent?",
              "Authoritative?",
              "Corroborated?"
            ],
            "largeText": true
